      "hardware_label": "2x RTX 3060 12GB",
      "notes": "T7810 (Dell Precision T7810), Dual Intel Xeon E5-2650 v4 (2x12c/24t, 2.20GHz), 32GB DDR4 ECC 2133 MT/s (8x4GB), PCIe Gen 3 x16 (8GT/s), both GPUs on same NUMA node (NUMA 0, PHB topology). vLLM v0.24.0, PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130, CUDA 13.0. Tensor parallel TP=2 across both RTX 3060s. AWQ INT4 (compressed-tensors, group_size=32). GPU mem util 85%. Flash attn v2. Qwen3.5 hybrid SSM: 32 layers, 8 full attn, 24 SSM. GQA 4 KV heads, head_dim=256. Concurrency sweep (batch 1-10, 128 tok): conc=1: 80.9 t/s/req, 80.9 t/s aggregate; conc=2: 62.2 t/s/req, 124.6 t/s aggregate; conc=3: 71.9 t/s/req, 216.0 t/s aggregate; conc=4: 69.0 t/s/req, 276.1 t/s aggregate; conc=5: 64.2 t/s/req, 321.3 t/s aggregate; conc=6: 42.1 t/s/req, 252.5 t/s aggregate; conc=7: 60.0 t/s/req, 419.6 t/s aggregate; conc=8: 60.0 t/s/req, 479.7 t/s aggregate; conc=9: 53.3 t/s/req, 479.7 t/s aggregate; conc=10: 52.7 t/s/req, 527.4 t/s aggregate. Aggregate scales 80.9 to 527.4 t/s (6.5x). TTFT flat ~70ms. Sweet spot conc=5 or 8.",
